# LLM Prompt Injection Test Cases

## Objective

This project explores common prompt-injection patterns in LLM
applications in an authorized testing environment.

## Tests

### 1. Instruction Override

Attempts to make the model disregard previously established
instructions.

### 2. System Instruction Request

Tests whether an application unnecessarily reveals hidden
system instructions.

### 3. Role Manipulation

Attempts to change the model's assumed role and bypass
application-level restrictions.

## Security Considerations

A secure LLM application should treat untrusted user input as
untrusted data and maintain a clear separation between system
instructions and user-controlled content.

Testing should only be performed against systems for which the
tester has authorization.
